# MP2 correlation energy for helium.
#
# Same `cc2` parameter group as the CC2 workflow -- MP2 is `calc_type mp2`
# within it, and `--wf=mp2` is an alias for the same chain. Results land in
# tasks[1] as mp2_correlation_energy / mp2_total_energy.
#
# Fixed `k`: the correlated step needs the reference at a single resolution, so
# there is no `protocol` ladder here (a reference that climbed the ladder mixes
# resolutions and aborts in the tensor layer).
#
# Reference provenance: mp2_correlation_energy = -0.0373696920703866, generated
# 2026-07-30 on node26. The 2025 value in the retired
# test_mp2_helium.py reference (-0.0374699766577594) came from identical settings
# and is stale by 1e-4 -- code drift in the correlated step, not a settings
# difference; the SCF energies agree to 6e-8. Do not "restore" the old number.
#
# The 1e-4 tolerance on the correlated quantities is a judgement call, not a
# measurement: SCF energies here reproduce across macOS/clang/Accelerate and
# Linux/GNU-13/MKL to 5e-16, but no 6D correlated run has been compared across
# architectures. If it proves too tight the symptom is a spurious failure on a
# new platform, which beats missing a regression -- widen it then, deliberately.
#
# Run:   ./run.sh          (or: madqc --wf=mp2 mp2_he_corr.in)

dft
    xc       hf
    k        5
    maxiter  10
    econv    1e-5
    dconv    1e-3
end

cc2
    freeze     0
    calc_type  mp2
end

molecule
    units   atomic
    He  0.0  0.0  0.0
end
